# Secrets and per-deployment overrides for pinakesd. Copy to .env, fill in what you use, and load
# it before starting the daemon (see "Configuration and secrets" in README.md). Every value here
# is a placeholder. Never commit .env.
#
# Any config key can be set as PINAKES__SECTION__KEY; the environment wins over the TOML file.
# Unknown keys stop startup.

# --- Database ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The full connection URL, password included; it replaces database_url from the TOML file. A
# peer-authenticated Unix socket needs no password (postgresql:///pinakes?host=/var/run/postgresql).
# PINAKES__DATABASE_URL=postgresql://pinakes:change-me@db.example.internal:5432/pinakes

# --- Admin listener ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bearer token for every admin route (metrics, operator info, the stored document, curation).
# Required when admin_listen is not a loopback address; recommended always. An empty token is
# refused at startup, so leave the line commented until it has a value (a long random string).
# PINAKES__ADMIN_TOKEN=change-me

# --- Logging ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Log filter in tracing's EnvFilter syntax; logs are JSON lines on standard output. The default:
# RUST_LOG=pinakes=info,pinakes_core=info,sqlx=warn

# --- Overrides (examples) ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any limit from docs/operations.md:
# PINAKES__LIMITS__RESOLVER_CONCURRENCY=8
# A per-host request rate (requests per second). The host name keeps its dots, which systemd
# EnvironmentFile= and --env-file accept but a shell cannot source; from a shell, set it in
# [limits.host_rates] in the TOML file instead.
# PINAKES__LIMITS__HOST_RATES__api.example.org=0.5
